wner account. (eg. `address(0)`)"}],"OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(address)":[{"details":"The caller account is not authorized to perform an operation."}],"ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall()":[{"details":"Unauthorized reentrant call."}],"SafeERC20FailedOperation(address)":[{"details":"An operation with an ERC-20 token failed."}]},"kind":"dev","methods":{"clearSplitForPath(address[])":{"details":"Deletes the stored SplitCfg for this path key.         After clearing, split will not be applied.","params":{"path":"Exact swap path to clear"}},"getAmountsOut(uint256,address[])":{"details":"Behavior:         - If `path` is a direct Curve 3Pool stable->stable swap (length == 2):              if path.length == 2 and both tokens are 3Pool stables, uses Curve 3Pool quote only;               returns empty array if Curve quote fails (no fallback)         - For V2 routers:              selects the best quote among supported routers              if oracle data is available & fresh, returns empty array when the best DEX quote              is worse than oracle by more than `maxDeviationBps`         - Returns empty array if no supported router can quote or quoting fails","params":{"amountIn":"Input amount (raw decimals of `path[0]`)","path":"Swap path (length >= 2)"},"returns":{"amounts":" Standard V2 amounts array, or empty array if no acceptable route"}},"owner()":{"details":"Returns the address of the current owner."},"renounceOwnership()":{"details":"Leaves the contract without owner. It will not be possible to call `onlyOwner` functions. Can only be called by the current owner. NOTE: Renouncing ownership will leave the contract without an owner, thereby disabling any functionality that is only available to the owner."},"rescueTokens(address,address,uint256)":{"params":{"amount":"Amount to transfer","to":"Recipient address","token":"ERC20 token address"}},"setAsEthLike(address,bool)":{"params":{"isAsEth":"If true, use ETH-denominated route for oracle price","token":"Token address"}},"setOracleConfig(uint16,uint256)":{"params":{"deviationBps":"Max allowed negative deviation vs oracle in bps","maxStaleness":"Acceptable feed age in seconds (0 = skip staleness check)"}},"setSplitForPath(address[],bool,uint256,uint16)":{"details":"Path key is computed as keccak256(abi.encode(path)).         If `threshold == 0`, split is considered \"not configured\".         Split is applied only when:           - enabled == true           - amountIn >= threshold           - a second distinct router has a valid quote","params":{"bpsA":"Share of first router in basis points (0..10000)","enabled":"Whether split is enabled for this path","path":"Exact swap path (length >= 2)","threshold":"Minimum amountIn required to trigger splitting"}},"setdefaultSlippageBpsCurve3(uint16)":{"params":{"newBps":"New slippage in basis points (0..10000)"}},"setdefaultSlippageBpsV2(uint16)":{"params":{"newBps":"New slippage in basis points (0..10000)"}},"swapExactTokensForTokens(uint256,uint256,address[],address,uint256)":{"details":"High-level flow:         1) If `path` is a direct Curve 3Pool stable->stable swap (length == 2):              - uses `CURVE3POOL.exchange(i, j, amountIn, minOutUsed)`              - if `amountOutMin == 0`, computes `minOutUsed` from Curve quote using `defaultSlippageBpsCurve3`              - if oracle data is available & fresh, reverts if Curve quote is worse than oracle                by more than `maxDeviationBps`              - transfers final tokenOut to `to`         2) Otherwise (V2 routers Uni/Sushi):              - finds top-1 and top-2 router quotes among supported venues              - applies split only when the per-path SplitCfg is enabled AND:                    * threshold > 0                    * amountIn >= threshold                    * a second distinct router exists with a valid quote              - if `amountOutMin == 0`, computes per-leg minOut using `defaultSlippageBpsV2`              - if oracle data is available & fresh, reverts if the expected DEX output                (single quote or sum of re-quotes in split) is worse than oracle by more than `maxDeviationBps`              - pulls `amountIn` from msg.sender, approves router(s), executes swap(s) sending outputs to `to`","params":{"amountIn":"Exact tokens to swap (pulled from msg.sender)","amountOutMin":"Global minimum acceptable output (0 => compute local minOut from quotes + default slippage)","deadline":"Unix timestamp after which the tx must revert","path":"Swap path (length >= 2)","to":"Recipient of output tokens"},"returns":{"amounts":"     If split: [amountIn, totalOut]; otherwise: V2 router amounts array"}},"swapExactTokensForTokensWithReport(uint256,uint256,address[],address,uint256)":{"params":{"amountIn":"Exact tokens to swap (taken from `msg.sender`)","amountOutMin":"Global minimum final out (if 0, local minOuts are computed)","deadline":"Unix timestamp after which the tx must revert","path":"Swap path (length >= 2)","to":"Recipient of output tokens"},"returns":{"amounts":"        If split: [amountIn, totalOut]; else the router's V2 array","minOutUsed":"     MinOut actually enforced in this call (sum of legs if split)","quotedOutGross":" Baseline best quote (no split, no slippage deduction)"}},"transferOwnership(address)":{"details":"Transfers ownership of the contract to a new account (`newOwner`). Can only be called by the current owner."}},"title":"DexV2AggregatorModuleMk4","version":1},"userdoc":{"events":{"OracleConfigUpdated(uint16,uint256)":{"notice":"Oracle config update (registry is constant; here we only emit the values that can change)"}},"kind":"user","methods":{"CURVE3POOL()":{"notice":"Curve 3Pool instance (DAI/USDC/USDT) used for stable-to-stable fast-path swaps (mainnet 3pool)"},"DENOM_ETH()":{"notice":"Chainlink denominations (as per Feed Registry)"},"FEED_REGISTRY()":{"notice":"Chainlink Feed Registry (Ethereum mainnet)"},"asEthLike(address)":{"notice":"Tokens priced \"as ETH\" (e.g., WETH, stETH, wstETH)"},"clearSplitForPath(address[])":{"notice":"Remove split configuration for a given path"},"constructor":{"notice":"Initializes the module owner."},"defaultSlippageBpsV2()":{"notice":"Default slippage applied when caller passes `amountOutMin == 0` (in bps)"},"getAmountsOut(uint256,address[])":{"notice":"V2-compatible `getAmountsOut` with best-effort oracle guard filtering"},"maxDeviationBps()":{"notice":"Oracle guard configuration"},"rescueTokens(address,address,uint256)":{"notice":"Emergency token withdrawal by the owner"},"setAsEthLike(address,bool)":{"notice":"Mark/unmark token to be priced \"as ETH\" in oracle math"},"setOracleConfig(uint16,uint256)":{"notice":"Set oracle configuration (deviation, staleness)"},"setSplitForPath(address[],bool,uint256,uint16)":{"notice":"Configure split settings for an exact swap path"},"setdefaultSlippageBpsCurve3(uint16)":{"notice":"Update the default slippage Curve3 bps used when `amountOutMin == 0`"},"setdefaultSlippageBpsV2(uint16)":{"notice":"Update the default slippage V2 bps used when `amountOutMin == 0`"},"splitForPath(bytes32)":{"notice":"Per-path split settings (key = keccak256(abi.encode(path)))"},"swapExactTokensForTokens(uint256,uint256,address[],address,uint256)":{"notice":"Execute an exact-in swap with optional auto-split and best-effort oracle guard"},"swapExactTokensForTokensWithReport(uint256,uint256,address[],address,uint256)":{"notice":"Same as `swapExactTokensForTokens`, but also returns:         (a) baseline gross quote (top-1) and (b) the actual minOut used"}},"notice":"Aggregates UniV2/SushiV2 quotes, can auto-split execution across top-2 venues,         and applies a best-effort Chainlink Feed Registry guard when oracle data is available & fresh.","version":1}},"settings":{"compilationTarget":{"contracts/swap/DexV2AggregatorModuleMk4.sol":"DexV2AggregatorModuleMk4"},"evmVersion":"osaka","libraries":{},"metadata":{"bytecodeHash":"ipfs"},"optimizer":{"enabled":true,"runs":20},"remappings":[],"viaIR":true},"sources":{"@op